  "details": "This might feel like off topic, but as resent Age Verification FAQ clearly states intents to integrate it with Content Gating System, i.e. make some content loadable only if they contain no adult labels for general non-verified audience.\n\nThis is **too radical to make whole avatars and worlds unloadable** if they got (have to be) labeled just because some insignificant parts of it is NSFW, so...\n\nMay be just expose that info to the avatar animators and world scripts? So, they can dynamically adjust their rendering content to the gating settings?\n\nFor example, avatar may hide for gated local users something like blood, cigarettes, other kind of items, lock some animation states, etc.\n\nWorlds can replace some assets to a different kind as, for example, in TF2 in Germany it was confetti instead of gore. 🤷‍♂",
